-- Transcription of layout-language-consult.md §5.4 (lines 545-583),
-- clean-room LengYue, landscape class. Disclosed adjustments:
--   - no-op root sizing supplied (document elides it, same as all five
--     encodings — see q5go.lyt's comment for the full reasoning).
--   - `T(...)[BLACK BOX]{pref 1fr, min envelope over tabs}`: the bare
--     "min envelope over tabs" prose isn't a literal value, so 'min' is
--     omitted here and the compiler derives the T-node's structural
--     minimum as the componentwise max of its children (§4.1 line
--     298-302).
--   - the five bare `CP-library, CP-cards, CP-settings, CP-analysis,
--     CP-other` names inside T(...) (line 576) aren't bracketed
--     `widgetid[domain,...]` leaves at all — they're prose naming the
--     control-panel tabs, which §2 explicitly commissions as an opaque
--     black box outside the A/go|common|debug|board classification. We
--     give each one domain='blackbox' (the sixth domain literal added in
--     lyt_ast.py specifically for this region) and no facets.
--   - `A_go[go, action]{28px}`, `A_common[common, action]{28px}`: the
--     bare-fixed-extent shorthand (min=pref=max=28px).
--   - `I_engine[...]{28px, envelope: {...}}`: fixed 28px reservation with
--     an attached (documentation-only, for this 1-D sizing model) content
--     state list; states renamed to valid identifiers
--     (`connected_5digit_latency` for the document's
--     "connected×latency≤5digits", since '×' and '≤' aren't legal
--     identifier characters).
--   - F4 DISCLOSURE (review row 1609,
--     .claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-compiler-prototype-review.md finding
--     F4 item 4): every one of the T(...)'s children below is given
--     its own `min WRAPPER_MIN` (300px). §5.4's own text (line 577) gives
--     no such per-child min — the bare "min envelope over tabs" phrase is
--     prose, not a value, and the compiler derives the T-node's OWN
--     structural min as the componentwise max of its children's declared
--     mins (§4.1 line 298-302). Left with no per-child min at all, that
--     derivation would yield T's own min = 0px, which reads as "the
--     black-box region gets no floor at all" — an equally unfaithful
--     reading of the same prose. We import WRAPPER_MIN onto every child
--     instead, so the derived T floor is a real, if approximate, 300px —
--     the SAME choice lengyue_portrait.lyt already makes (with 200px,
--     disclosed there).
--   - AMENDMENT 3 (ledger row 1715, gap-amendment-build): three `gap`
--     declarations, all mapped onto `frontend/src/assets/css/theme.css`'s
--     `--space-*` tier scale (that file's own §"Four tiers for gap,
--     padding, margin", read in full):
--       - the OUTER H(...) (boardRail vs. board area vs. the side control
--         column) gets `gap 12px`, `--space-medium` ("section-level gap,
--         content-block separation") — for the split between the page's
--         MAJOR REGIONS. DISCLOSED DOWN-TIER FROM `--space-loose` (20px),
--         per the original build report's finding (900x600 regresses to
--         INFEASIBLE at the wider tier); unchanged by the additions
--         below.
--       - the side column's own V(...) (the go-actions/engine-info/
--         common-actions strip stack feeding the tree/panels row) keeps
--         `gap 4px`, `--space-tight` ("button-cluster gaps, icon
--         spacing, tight rows").
--       - NEW: the tree/panels/preview row (see the "TREE ALWAYS
--         VISIBLE" note below) is itself an H(...) needing its own gap
--         between tree, the control-panel tab group, and the preview
--         board — `gap 4px`, `--space-tight` again, matching the
--         side column's own tier (this row IS one of the side column's
--         "tight rows").
--
--   - TREE ALWAYS VISIBLE (ledger row ~1735, commissioner review of the
--     clean-room mockups: "'Tree & Panels' look like it has tabs, one
--     for tree and one for the other stuff in the control panel, but the
--     tree should always be visible"). The tree leaf is pulled OUT of
--     the T(...) exclusive group and made a permanent sibling of it,
--     inside a new H(...) row: `H(tree, T(CP-*), previewBoard)`. This
--     is NOT a new invention — it reproduces, almost exactly, the SHAPE
--     the as-is encoding already transcribes for the real app
--     (`encodings/current_row_asis.lyt`'s own
--     `H(tree{140px,drag-persisted}, resizerInner, T(CP-*){WRAPPER_MIN})`
--     — this file omits the resizer leaf, since the census census
--     doesn't carry a dedicated resizer widget in this consolidated
--     tree, and drops `drag-persisted` since this prototype's L4
--     accounting is unimplemented (README.md's L4 section) and neither
--     clean-room encoding used it before). Tree's reservation, 140px
--     fixed (`min=pref=max=140px`), is grounded directly in
--     `frontend/src/state/layout-model.ts`'s `TREE_PANEL_MIN_WIDTH_PX`
--     AND `TREE_PANEL_DEFAULT_WIDTH_PX` (both 140, the row-axis policy
--     object every width class currently shares) — the "sensible
--     reservation" the commission asked to ground against the live app.
--     The T(...) node keeps `{pref 1fr}` (elastic, min still derived from
--     its now-five children's own WRAPPER_MIN, unchanged), and picks up
--     what's left of the row after tree, the tight gaps, and the new
--     preview board below claim their fixed shares. The T node's own
--     `[BLACK BOX]` tag is, if anything, MORE accurate now than before —
--     every one of its remaining children is domain='blackbox', where
--     previously the tag covered tree too (domain='board', never
--     actually blackbox).
--
--   - boardRail (ledger row 1735, commissioner ruling: "the clean-room
--     encodings OMITTED the boardRail... it returns as a
--     USER-TOGGLEABLE presence slot — user-initiated, space-releasing
--     ... wired into the corner presence-menu... DEFAULT OFF"). Identity
--     and ~168px reservation grounded in
--     `encodings/current_row_asis.lyt`'s own transcription: that file's
--     `@toggle(user, release) {min 168px, pref 168px, max 168px} V(
--     loadSave, boardRail, addBoard, jankTest, preview )` is the real
--     app's sidebar rail. This clean-room file, being function-
--     consolidated (per the original commission), does not carry
--     loadSave/addBoard/jankTest/preview as separate leaves — those are
--     out of THIS commission's naming (only "boardRail (the open-boards
--     thumbnail rail)" was named), so only `boardRail` itself is added,
--     at the SAME 168px width the whole rail column occupied (the one
--     concrete number the ruling supplies: "reservation grounded in the
--     as-is encoding's value"). Placement: leftmost child of the root
--     H(...), i.e. "the left edge as today" — the ruling's own
--     conservative default, unchanged from the as-is app's real DOM
--     order (`App.vue`'s sidebar rail sits left of the main H, before
--     the toggle rail even). Presence (`@toggle`, release, DEFAULT OFF)
--     is NOT expressed in this file's own concrete syntax — like the
--     rest of this encoding (see the pre-existing header note below,
--     "Neither `.lyt` source file declares an `@toggle` presence"), the
--     corner presence-menu is a generator-level (`emit_mockup.py`
--     `TOGGLE_TARGETS`) affordance layered on top of an otherwise
--     `@fixed` AST; boardRail's toggle registration, presence type, and
--     default-hidden state all live there, disclosed in that module's
--     own docstring.
--
--   - previewBoard (ledger row 1735, SECOND commissioner amendment: "a
--     variation-preview mini board (lizzieyzy / chess-preview paradigm),
--     LOWER RIGHT of the layout... aspect-1 leaf... modest reservation,
--     grounded against the existing library MiniBoard's 160x160
--     precedent... user-toggleable... DEFAULT OFF"). Placement: the
--     rightmost slot of the new tree/panels row (`H(tree, T(CP-*),
--     previewBoard)`) — that row is the bottom-most element of the side
--     column, which is itself the page's rightmost region in landscape,
--     so its own rightmost slot IS the page's lower-right corner
--     (already home to the corner presence-menu button per the prior
--     build report's own WITNESSED claim #4). Reservation: 160px fixed
--     on BOTH axes (`min=pref=max=160px, aspect 1`), the exact square
--     grounded in `frontend/src/components/library/LibraryPreviewPane.
--     vue`'s own "160×160 box (both dimensions capped, not just width)"
--     precedent (that file's own comment, read in full). This is the
--     SECOND aspect-locked leaf in this program (the board `B` is the
--     first) — `compiler.py`'s aspect-slack machinery
--     (`_collect_aspect_slack_terms`, Stage 1.5) is written generically
--     over every aspect leaf in the tree, not hardcoded to one, so no
--     compiler change was needed; `emit_mockup.py`'s own board-only
--     `is_board_leaf` cross-axis-containment check was generalized to
--     `is_aspect_leaf` (any leaf with a declared `aspect`, not just
--     widget id `"B"`) for the same reason on the generator side — see
--     that module's own docstring for the disclosure.
--
--     DESIGN NOTE (Vue-realization phase, no build action taken here):
--     the commissioner separately floated boardRail-as-POPOVER (overlay
--     stratum, zero standing cost, triggered from chrome) as an
--     alternative to the presence-slot shape built here. Recorded as an
--     open fork for whoever picks up the eventual Vue implementation —
--     this commission was explicitly to keep building the presence-slot
--     version.
layout lengyue-landscape =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 12px} H(
    {min 168px, pref 168px, max 168px} boardRail[common, info+action],
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {pref maximize, aspect 1} B[board],
      {min 24px, pref 24px, max 24px} I_board[board, info],
      {min 28px, pref 28px, max 28px} A_board[board, action]
    ),
    {min 340px, pref 32fr, max 340px+60ch, gap 4px} V(
      {28px} A_go[go, action],
      {28px, envelope: {disconnected, connected_5digit_latency}} I_engine[common, info],
      {28px} A_common[common, action],
      {pref 1fr, gap 4px} H(
        {min 140px, pref 140px, max 140px} tree[board, info+action],
        {pref 1fr} T(
          {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-library[blackbox],
          {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-cards[blackbox],
          {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-settings[blackbox],
          {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-analysis[blackbox],
          {min WRAPPER_MIN, pref 1fr, max inf} CP-other[blackbox]
        )[BLACK BOX],
        {min 160px, pref 160px, max 160px, aspect 1} previewBoard[common, info]
      )
    )
  )
